# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows may rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout. For a shell script that
# is not cosmetic: a CRLF shebang makes Linux report "bad interpreter", which
# is a confusing failure to hit on a Pi at deployment time. Pin the files
# whose endings are functional.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
